# ===========================================================================
#  .mailmap — canonicalise author identities
# ===========================================================================
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   `git shortlog`, `git log --format='%aN'` and other tooling show one entry
#   per distinct author *string*. Without this file a single person appears as
#   several, which splits their commit counts. The individual 10% sprint
#   component is read off commit history, so identities must be canonical
#   BEFORE a marker reads them.
#
# WHAT IT DOES AND DOES NOT DO
#   It is a DISPLAY layer only. It does NOT rewrite history — a raw
#   `git log --format='%ae'` still shows the original address. Use the
#   mailmap-aware forms (`%aN`, `%aE` — capital letter) to see canonical values.
#
# FORMAT
#   Canonical Name <canonical@email>  Alias Name <alias@email>
#   Canonical Name <canonical@email>  <alias@email>
#
# TO ADD YOURSELF
#   Add one line per alias you have committed under. Verify with:
#       git shortlog -sne --all
# ===========================================================================

